# DUMP - Inspect file bytes

```text
DUMP file [/P] [/FROM=offset] [/LEN=count]
```

## Display a range

DUMP shows file offsets, hexadecimal bytes and printable characters.
/FROM and /LEN are hexadecimal. This displays 16 bytes starting at
offset 20H.

```text
B0:DUMP D0:IMAGE.COM /FROM=20 /LEN=10
```

## Browse and find

/P opens the paged viewer with a supported screen backend. G goes to an
offset. F asks for a search pattern and its type (hex bytes or ASCII).
After a find, period repeats it forward and comma repeats it backward.
/40 selects the narrow layout.
